#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

void bc_close(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Closes the connection to the \f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R] instance and
frees all resources associated with the client handle \f[CR]c\f[R].
.PP
The function performs the following steps in order:
.IP "1." 3
Sends a disconnect message on \f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R] (best\-effort;
errors are ignored since the connection may already be broken).
.IP "2." 3
Closes the underlying transport (socket, pipe, or file descriptor).
.IP "3." 3
For stdio transport, terminates the child subprocess
(\f[CR]SIGTERM\f[R], followed by \f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R] after a grace period
if needed).
.IP "4." 3
Frees all internal buffers and the handle itself.
.PP
After \f[CR]bc_close\f[R] returns, the pointer \f[CR]c\f[R] is invalid
and must not be used.
.PP
It is safe to call \f[CR]bc_close\f[R] with a NULL argument; the
function returns immediately without action.
